		<title type="html"><![CDATA[FYI. Battery life]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2427&amp;p=20127#p20127"><![CDATA[
FYI<br><br>I measured the current consumed by the UV380 when in its power saving phase as part of the Eco modes, and the current consumed was 33mA.<br><br>Under the same conditions, the GD-77 only consumes 19mA.<br><br>So the battery life of the UV380 / RT-3S will probably be about 30% worse than the GD-77<br><br>It may be possible to reduce the current consumption of the UV380 / RT-3S slighly by configuring the display controller into its power saving mode, as I think the display controller takes 6mA, howerver there are many other more important things that need to be fixed on the UV380/RT-3S<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Oct 16, 2022 10:04 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
